# Order of Operations: TRANSFORM fires before FOLLOW (moveblock).
# Wiki: object transformations (IS) happen in step 3; FOLLOW is in moveblock, step 5.
# If a FOLLOW target transforms away (changes kind) before FOLLOW fires, the follower
# finds no matching target and does not move.
#
# Setup: keke at (5,5). Rock at (8,5), 3 tiles to the right.
# ROCK IS FOLLOW KEKE: rock follows keke.
# KEKE IS BABA: keke transforms to baba this tick. After transform, no keke exists.
#
# Correct order (TRANSFORM then FOLLOW):
#   TRANSFORM: keke at (5,5) → baba at (5,5). No keke objects remain.
#   FOLLOW: "ROCK IS FOLLOW KEKE" — no keke in world → rock has no target → rock stays at (8,5).
#   Result: rock at (8,5), baba at (5,5).
#
# Wrong order (FOLLOW then TRANSFORM — the bug in our engine):
#   FOLLOW: keke still exists at (5,5). Rock at (8,5) moves one step LEFT toward keke → (7,5).
#   TRANSFORM: keke → baba.
#   Result: rock at (7,5) — assertion "at 8 5 rock" would FAIL.

[setup]
version 1
name "oop: transform before follow (follow sees post-transform state)"

text 0 0 keke
text 1 0 is
text 2 0 baba

text 0 1 rock
text 1 1 follow
text 2 1 keke

object 5 5 keke right
object 8 5 rock right

[inputs]
wait

[expected]
at 5 5 baba
not_at 5 5 keke
at 8 5 rock
not_won
